## 10. Mobile Authentication — Current Wiring (DO NOT BREAK)

**Status:** Stable as of Apr 21, 2026 (APRIL_2026_FIXES.md #127, #127.1, #127.2). This section documents exactly what is wired so future changes don't regress it. Before modifying ANY auth code, read this section, then read `apps/mobile/hooks/useSignInHandlers.ts` end-to-end. Do not "simplify", "modernize", or "refactor" the reset calls, the SSO name-collection fallback, or the `signUp.password()` invocation without re-reading the history below.

### 10.1 Architecture Summary

Mobile auth is a **custom Clerk integration** (not Clerk's prebuilt `<SignIn>` / `<SignUp>` components — those are web-only). The web app uses `@clerk/nextjs`'s prebuilt components which auto-handle missing-field collection + legal consent; mobile has to replicate that behavior by hand. That asymmetry is intentional and permanent — do NOT try to add Clerk's prebuilt UI to Expo.

- **Hook:** `apps/mobile/hooks/useSignInHandlers.ts` — single source of truth for ALL sign-in / sign-up logic (email+password, SSO, name collection).
- **Screen:** `apps/mobile/app/sign-in.tsx` — orchestrates UI state, renders the correct sub-component based on `pendingSSONameProvider`.
- **Sub-components:** `apps/mobile/components/sign-in/*` — `AppleOAuthButton`, `OAuthButton` (Google), `CredentialsForm`, `SSONameCollection`, `TermsDisclaimer`, `VerificationCodeInput`, etc.

### 10.2 The Three Sign-Up Paths (and what each one touches)

1. **Email + Password sign-up** (`onEmailSignUp`):
   - Calls `signUp.password({ emailAddress, password, firstName, lastName, legalAccepted: true })` (Clerk v3 API — **not** `signUp.create()`).
   - `legalAccepted: true` is passed programmatically because the Clerk Dashboard has "Require legal acceptance" enabled. See `TermsDisclaimer` (clickwrap pattern).
   - **Defensive reset at the top of `onEmailSignUp` is MANDATORY.** Before calling `signUp.password()`, we call `resetClerkSignUp(signUp)` to clear any stale `sua_*` id held over from an abandoned SSO attempt. Removing this reset re-introduces the "No sign up was found with id sua_*" regression.
2. **SSO (Apple / Google)** (`runSSOFlow`):
   - Calls `startSSOFlow({ strategy })` from `useSSO()`.
   - If `createdSessionId` is set → existing user, `setActive()` + navigate. Done.
   - If `signUp` is returned with `status: "missing_requirements"`:
     - If `legal_accepted` is missing → call `ssoSignUp.update({ legalAccepted: true })` (programmatic consent, per the clickwrap disclaimer already shown).
     - If `first_name` or `last_name` is still missing → stash `ssoSignUp` in `ssoSignUpRef` and set `pendingSSONameProvider`. This triggers the UI to render `<SSONameCollection>`, which collects the names and calls `onCompleteSSONameCollection(firstName, lastName)` → `ssoSignUp.update({ firstName, lastName })` → `setActive()`.
     - If still incomplete after all known remedies → call `resetClerkSignUp(currentSignUp)` and surface the error.
3. **SSO name-collection cancellation** (`cancelSSONameCollection`):
   - Called when the user backs out of `<SSONameCollection>`.
   - **Fire-and-forget `resetClerkSignUp(abandoned)` is MANDATORY.** Skipping it re-introduces the stale `sua_*` bug when the user then switches to email signup.

### 10.3 Why Apple Sign-In Triggers the Name-Collection Screen

Apple releases first/last name **only once per Apple ID per app** — on the very first authorization. On every subsequent Apple Sign-In (even in simulators, even after "Stop Using Apple ID" in system settings), Apple returns the email but withholds names. Clerk then flags `first_name` + `last_name` as `missingFields` and our UI renders `<SSONameCollection>`. This is expected behavior, matches how Spotify / Uber / Lyft handle the same Apple quirk, and must not be "fixed" by removing the screen.

### 10.4 `__internal_future.reset()` — Why We Use It

- `SignUpResource.__internal_future.reset()` is a local-only state clear on the Clerk client. It does NOT hit the network and is safe to call on fresh state.
- We deliberately avoid `client.signUp.destroy()` — that attempts a server-side DELETE and 404s when the `sua_*` id has already been consumed or never existed.
- The `__internal_future` namespace is Clerk's internal API. Call sites are narrow (`resetClerkSignUp` helper, 3 invocations) and structurally typed via `SSOSignUpHandle`. If Clerk removes this API in a future SDK bump, `resetClerkSignUp` will silently no-op (the optional-chain guards + try/catch) — verify at that point and migrate.

### 10.5 Terms & Conditions — One Disclaimer, Always Visible

- `<TermsDisclaimer />` is rendered **unconditionally** below `<CredentialsForm>` in `sign-in.tsx`.
- It is a **clickwrap** — the user's act of tapping "Continue with Apple" / "Continue with Google" / "Sign up" / "Sign in" is the legal agreement. `legalAccepted: true` is passed programmatically.
- There is no longer a `TermsCheckbox` — do NOT re-add one. The clickwrap pattern is the intentionally simplified single consent surface (see APRIL_2026_FIXES.md #127.1).

### 10.6 Known Edge Case (Deferred)

Deleting an account in-session and immediately trying to re-register (without closing the app) can still hit `No sign up was found with id sua_*`. Logged as edge case #92 in `EDGE_CASES_TODOS.MD`. Workaround: force-quit + relaunch. Rare enough to defer; do NOT chase it as part of unrelated work.

### 10.7 Checklist Before Touching This Code

- [ ] Re-read `useSignInHandlers.ts` top-to-bottom.
- [ ] Re-read `APRIL_2026_FIXES.md` #127, #127.1, #127.2 for historical context.
- [ ] If removing/moving `resetClerkSignUp` calls — stop. Each of the three call sites exists to prevent a specific regression. Find a different path.
- [ ] If changing `signUp.password()` to `signUp.create()` or similar — stop. `password()` is the Clerk v3 API (APRIL_2026_FIXES.md #125). `create()` was the legacy v2 method.
- [ ] If adding a `TermsCheckbox` back — stop. The clickwrap disclaimer is intentional.
- [ ] Test every auth path after changes: (a) new email signup, (b) existing email sign-in, (c) Apple first-time, (d) Apple returning-user (triggers name-collection screen), (e) Google first-time, (f) Google returning-user, (g) SSO → back out of name collection → email signup (stale-id regression check).
